Answer the following computer science question. The last line of your response should be of the following format: 'Answer: $LETTER' (without quotes) where LETTER is one of ABCD.

What constitutes a valid definition of an interface named Transportable, provided that there is already a valid interface called Movable?

A.  interface Transportable extends Movable { /*…*/ }
B.  interface Transportable implements Movable { /*…*/ }
C.  class Movable implements Transportable { /*…*/ }
D.  class Movable extends Transportable { /*…*/ }

